  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$C_1:(x+3)^2+(y+3)^2=3^2$<br/><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/3NdJSVTBZnaQslvzzf-ePANNRDktQsHIAYcBi43TarU.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>Let $\\mathrm{C}_1$ and $\\mathrm{C}_2$ has centres $A\\left(-3_1-3\\right)$ and $B(1,3)$<br/>$\\begin{aligned}<br/>& \\mathrm{AB}=\\sqrt{16+36}=2 \\sqrt{13} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{r}_1=3 \\text { and } \\mathrm{r}_2=2 \\sqrt{13}-3 \\\\\n& \\mathrm{P}(\\alpha, \\beta), \\alpha=\\frac{\\mathrm{r}_1(1)+\\mathrm{r}_2(-3)}{\\mathrm{r}_1+\\mathrm{r}_2}, \\beta=\\frac{\\mathrm{r}_1(3)+\\mathrm{r}_2(-3)}{\\mathrm{r}_1+\\mathrm{r}_2} \\\\\n& \\alpha=\\frac{3-3(2 \\sqrt{13}-3)}{2 \\sqrt{13}}, \\beta=\\frac{18-6 \\sqrt{13}}{2 \\sqrt{13}} \\\\\n& (\\beta-\\alpha)^2=\\left(\\frac{6}{2 \\sqrt{13}}\\right)^2 \\\\\n& (\\beta-\\alpha)^2=\\left(\\frac{6}{2 \\sqrt{13}}\\right)^2, \\mathrm{~m}+\\mathrm{n}=22<br/>\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
